# worker/.dev.vars — Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Gitignored.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (no extension), fill in the values, then
# (re)start wrangler dev. Cloudflare reads these only in local dev mode;
# production uses `wrangler secret put` for the same keys.
#
# Pull the same values that production already has by either:
#   1. Discord Developer Portal → your bot → Bot tab → Reset Token (then
#      `wrangler secret put DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN` to update prod with the new one
#      AND paste it here).
#   2. Or use the values you already have stored elsewhere (1Password, etc.).
#
# DO NOT commit .dev.vars. The .gitignore catches it.

# ── Required for /api/pick + /api/trade Discord posts ──────────────────
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=PASTE_YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE

# Optional override — defaults are baked into the worker code:
#   live=1059111651846131833 (#transactions)  test=1089538054236160010
# DISCORD_DRAFT_CHANNEL_ID=
# DISCORD_DRAFT_TEST_CHANNEL_ID=

# ── Required for /api/pick + /api/trade LIVE writes to MFL ─────────────
# (The simulate=true path doesn't need it.)
MFL_APIKEY=PASTE_YOUR_LEAGUE_APIKEY_HERE

# ── Commish gating ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated franchise IDs that get is_commish=true from /api/me.
# Drives the "Go LIVE" button visibility + LIVE-mode revert permission.
# Default if unset: just 0001.
COMMISH_FRANCHISE_IDS=0008

# ── Yahoo Fantasy OAuth (worker/src/yahoo_oauth.js) ────────────────────
# Only needed to exercise /admin/yahoo/* locally. Leave commented and those
# five routes REFUSE with a named error — they never fall back to a default.
# Register the app at https://developer.yahoo.com/apps/create/ with
# API Permissions → Fantasy Sports → Read (write access is unavailable from
# Yahoo in 2026 regardless of the scope you request).
#
# YAHOO_REDIRECT_URI must be BYTE-IDENTICAL to the Redirect URI registered on
# the Yahoo app — Yahoo compares it byte for byte and answers a mismatch with a
# bare 401 that looks like a credential problem. For `wrangler dev` that is
# usually http://localhost:8787/admin/yahoo/auth/callback.
#
# YAHOO_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY is base64 of exactly 32 bytes (AES-256-GCM):
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Missing / short / unparseable = the module refuses and the refresh token is
# never written. There is NO plaintext fallback, by design.
# YAHOO_CLIENT_ID=PASTE_YOUR_YAHOO_CLIENT_ID_HERE
# YAHOO_CLIENT_SECRET=PASTE_YOUR_YAHOO_CLIENT_SECRET_HERE
# YAHOO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8787/admin/yahoo/auth/callback
# YAHOO_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=PASTE_OPENSSL_RAND_BASE64_32_OUTPUT_HERE
